WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.470
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:14.380
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:21.130
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.830
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.930
You're on the other side of the table

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.300
I'm talking to you, but...

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:43.230
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:49.480
Even though I'm this close to you

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:56.750
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:03.490
What is truly precious?

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:12.980
Transcend Time!
Red-Eyes Black Metal Dragon

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:25.300
Good!  It's only a slight difference, but Jonouchi has taken the lead in life points!

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.260
You have to win, Jonouchi!

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:29.500
For Shizuka!

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.500
Jonouchi, keep going and take him down!

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:33.540
Right!

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.340
The flow of the game has turned in Jonouchi's favor.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:46.720
Even though Jonouchi boy is no match for Keith when it comes to experience and deck strength.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:50.000
What's allowing him to make up for that difference?

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.540
Oh, I see.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:06.300
After I defeated Keith, he drowned himself in booze and drugs.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:11.320
He fell so far that he competed in underground duels.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:14.910
On the other hand...

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.420
This is the symbol of our friendship.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.890
Even if we're apart, we're always united by this ring.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.310
How interesting.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:29.160
One is filled with despair and revenge.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:32.100
The other has hope and trust.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:36.700
Their mental battle is light and dark.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:43.470
Who will the goddess of victory smile upon in this duel?

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:49.410
What's so funny?

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:56.680
Kid, have you ever battled when you're on the brink of losing everything?

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:57.960
On the brink?

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:01.760
I'm asking if you've ever seen hell!

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.500
Have you tasted ultimate despair at the lowest point of existence?

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:10.670
The exit from my personal hell is right where Pegasus sits!

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.340
I'll do whatever it takes to crawl up there!

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:18.280
That's the lesson I learned in hell to survive!

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:20.210
What a bunch of garbage.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:21.880
What did you say?

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:29.320
I don't want to sound arrogant, but I do understand despair and revenge.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:34.460
But you've forgotten the more important thing in life!

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.130
What?

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:40.920
Too bad, but you won't reach Pegasus.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.280
Because I'm going to defeat you right here.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.070
It's your turn!

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:50.880
Keep talking.  I set one card.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:53.880
I'll take you on with this!

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:00.550
I'll give you a taste of hellish gambling.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:10.260
The cylinders of Barrel Dragon's triple gun cannons have a one-in-two chance of being loaded.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.200
One-in-two?

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:15.180
Let's go, Barrel Dragon.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.620
Gun Cannon Shot!

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:35.320
My monsters are all destroyed?

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:42.440
Barrel Dragon's gun cannons each have 2600 attack points.

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:47.260
It'll be kinda tough to avoid this simultaneous blast.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:50.480
It can attack up to three monsters simultaneously?

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.580
What a card!

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:55.210
No matter how many monsters he has, it won't be enough!

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:57.780
How interesting.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.140
In that case, I'll take you on with this card.

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:05.780
Time Wizard!

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:07.080
If you're gambling, I'll gamble too!

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:09.120
Time Wizard.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:11.800
That's Jonouchi's trump card!

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:16.330
If Time Roulette succeeds, it will corrode his Machine monster!

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:19.780
Oh, that's not the only card I'm bringing out.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:21.870
You're up, Baby Dragon!

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:27.760
It can combo with Time Wizard to transform into Thousand Dragon.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:31.380
And it'll destroy your lame Machine monster!

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:35.580
Here I go!  Time Roulette!

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:40.460
If the Roulette fails, Jonouchi's monsters will all be destroyed.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:43.520
And he'll lose life points equal to half their attack points.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:45.880
He's taking a big gamble for his fate.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:48.080
Please succeed.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.530
Show us your guts!

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:54.260
I'm counting on you, Time Wizard.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:06.140
The needle is stopping.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:13.280
All right!  Go!

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:16.290
Time Magic!

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:33.540
Jonouchi, attack now!

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.900
All right!  Go!

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:38.640
Thousand Nose Breath!

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:45.420
All right!  Barrel Dragon is destroyed!

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.560
Are you sure about that?

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:54.840
I told you that my deck is composed of invincible Machine cards.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.780
I activate my trap card!

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.230
A trap?

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.160
Time Machine!

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:09.270
What's that capsule?

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.040
The door is opening.

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:23.370
What?

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:28.990
Its attack and defense points have returned to normal.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:31.880
Go!  Gun Cannon Shot!

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:42.240
No way...  What happened?

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:52.800
When my monster is destroyed, Time Machine brings that monster back from the previous turn and lets it attack.

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:54.350
The monster from the previous turn?

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:59.720
If it's the Barrel Dragon before it became rusted, then its attack points wouldn't be decreased.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:04.290
I can't believe Jonouchi's special combo was defeated so easily.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:06.960
Keith is a powerful foe.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:12.480
I already know what's in your deck because I watched your duel against Kotsuzuka.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:16.770
And your amateur deck has no strategies.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:20.710
So he knows all my strategies?

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:23.710
Play a monster on your field.

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:30.220
I'll show you that your lame cards can't do a thing against my powerful Machine deck.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.820
I place a monster in defense position.

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:35.120
I end my turn.

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:39.060
If you're running away from confrontation, I'll play another monster.

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:42.060
I play a monster in attack position.

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:48.200
Barrel Dragon attacks your defending monster.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.670
Vanish, weakling!

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:58.020
I already have Red-Eyes in my hand.

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:03.820
But even if I use it to attack Slot Machine, Barrel Dragon will destroy it next turn.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:07.490
I can't bring out Red-Eyes so easily.

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:09.040
Jonouchi...

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:10.430
This match is one-sided.

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:12.700
Survive, Jonouchi.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:15.360
There must be a way to turn things around.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.300
I set one card on the field.

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:24.070
Next...

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:30.020
Red-Eyes B. Dragon in attack position!

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:34.780
I end my turn.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:42.660
That card has the most attack points in your deck, but it's still no match for my Barrel Dragon.

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:45.800
As you wish, I'll annihilate it!

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:50.300
Barrel Dragon, attack Red-Eyes!

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:54.860
Okay!  I flip over my set card!

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:55.570
What?

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:58.210
My set card is Copycat.

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:01.480
It copies one card you played.

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:05.080
I'll copy Magic Metal Force!

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:18.790
Red-Eyes Black Metal Dragon!

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:28.190
Nice!  His copy card will turn this match around!

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:31.810
Launch a counterattack!  Dark Mega Flare!

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:36.400
Barrel Dragon is destroyed!

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:44.720
Bandit Keith, as long as I can defeat you, I don't care if it's by luck or by a miracle!

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:49.080
If I win, Shizuka's eyes will be healed.

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:51.220
That's what I believe.

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:08.040
You won't be happy for long.

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.980
I have the strategies it takes to win.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:13.980
You're only managing to survive with your amateurish tricks.

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:16.920
They're not good enough to win.

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:20.860
The difference in our skills will determine who wins and who loses!

00:11:21.650 --> 00:11:25.760
Huh?  The difference in our skills?

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:29.030
But your life points have clearly decreased.

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:31.570
Keep talking!  It's my turn.

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:33.570
I set one card on the field.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:37.900
I switch Slot Machine to defense position and end my turn.

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:44.000
Since that Machine monster only has 2300 defense points, Red-Eyes can destroy it in a single attack.

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:47.180
My turn!

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:49.280
I set one card.

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:51.250
Attack Slot Machine!

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.020
Dark Mega Flare!

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:57.220
I'll use my set card.

00:11:57.220 --> 00:11:58.780
7 Completed!

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:05.900
Huh?  A seven appeared in Slot Machine's window.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:11.540
What?

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:17.440
This card is a power unit that raises Slot Machine's defense points.

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:22.120
Slot Machine gains 700 defense points, making it 3000.

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:24.400
Red-Eyes's attack won't work!

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:29.000
By deflecting my attack, I lose life points.

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:31.600
Jonouchi!

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:35.430
He'll now have to be careful in how he approaches Slot Machine.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:38.220
It's my turn.

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:44.870
I choose either attack or defense, and I can equip Slot Machine with up to three copies of 7 Completed.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:48.180
Including both attack and defense, that's a total of 2100 points.

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:53.410
I'll show you the true difference in our skills.

00:12:57.240 --> 00:13:00.710
I'll use my second 7 Completed this turn.

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:03.660
It raises its attack points by 700!

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:12.630
He's going to keep it in defense position while he raises its attack points.

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:13.880
This is bad.

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:19.640
If he uses one more 7 Completed on Slot Machine, it will have 3400 attack points.

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:21.580
Even Red-Eyes is no match for that.

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:24.130
I also play this card!

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:25.960
Blast Sphere!

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:35.190
What's that thing?

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:38.400
It will self-destruct on your next turn.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:41.360
It's a time bomb with 2900 attack points.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:42.960
What?

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:46.700
If it explodes, Red-Eyes will be destroyed!

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:52.080
I end my turn!

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:53.740
Your time is up, punk!

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:02.950
It's blown to pieces, you fool!

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:12.160
What?

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:16.600
That was close, but I survived thanks to this.

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:20.530
That Equip Card raised its attack points by 600?

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.260
He had me worried.

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:25.970
I can't believe I'm the one who lost life points!

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:27.500
I end my turn!

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:28.980
That punk!

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:34.350
I'll equip another 7 Completed on my turn.

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:37.520
I raise its attack points!

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:51.000
The monsters' attack points are equal.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:54.930
Jonouchi and Keith's life points are about the same too.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:58.100
The next turn will decide this match.

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:06.050
I have a card that can swap attack and defense points, but using it now will put me at a disadvantage.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:14.360
If you can't do anything, I'm going to take my turn.

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:18.980
I'll give you credit for making it this far.

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:21.000
But you'll go no further.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:22.730
Look at this card.

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:25.720
Pillager!

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:26.700
What?

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:31.600
Pillager lets me look at your hand and take one of your cards.

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:40.780
Let's see...

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.800
It swaps attack and defense points.

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:47.000
You have a nice card.

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:48.590
I'll take this one.

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:56.500
It's over, kid.

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:59.750
Shield & Sword!

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:06.580
I switch Slot Machine to attack position.

00:16:06.740 --> 00:16:08.540
Plasma Laser Cannon!

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:10.740
I flip over my set card!

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:12.010
That's pointless!

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:13.550
Fire!

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:18.440
I win-

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:20.820
What?

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:26.290
Graverobber?

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:30.360
You stole my Time Machine?

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:34.880
I don't really want to brag about my thieving skills.

00:16:39.820 --> 00:16:44.570
Time Machine brings a monster from the previous turn.

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:46.050
That means...

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:48.920
That's right.  One turn ago...

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:55.320
Red-Eyes Black Metal Dragon resurrects without its attack and defense points swapped!

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:07.830
Take this!  Dark Mega Flare!

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:14.640
No way!  How can I lose to that kid?

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:21.080
In the battle between hope and despair, the goddess of victory smiled upon hope.

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:22.510
Jonouchi!

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:25.450
Jonouchi is the winner!

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:29.420
I did it!

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:32.420
You did it, Jonouchi!

00:17:34.100 --> 00:17:35.820
I did it, Shizuka.

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:37.500
I did it, Mai.

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:39.930
This duel doesn't count!

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:42.400
Say what?

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:44.360
You don't know when to give up.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:48.410
His entry card didn't belong to him.

00:17:48.680 --> 00:17:52.710
That means he wasn't qualified to duel from the start!

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:54.260
You're right.

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:57.080
I couldn't find my card.

00:17:57.250 --> 00:17:59.900
But Mai gave me this card of hope.

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:03.920
But how did you know that this wasn't my card?

00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:06.000
Seems fishy.

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:08.360
So how did you know?

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:11.900
The answer is simple.

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:17.840
Bandit Keith, you stole Jonouchi boy's card.

00:18:18.620 --> 00:18:20.270
What?  How dare you!

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:22.060
Is that true?

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:24.710
Then you're the one we shouldn't forgive!

00:18:24.920 --> 00:18:31.120
I don't care which card belongs to whom.

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:36.910
But I cannot forgive cheating during this duel.

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:40.490
Cheating?

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:45.900
Keith, you hid 7 Completed cards in your wristband and added them to your hand.

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:50.940
Unfortunately, you cannot deceive my eyes.

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:53.370
Keith, how dare you!

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:56.310
He is banished from the kingdom.

00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:58.970
Let me go!

00:18:58.970 --> 00:19:00.910
Damn!  Pegasus!

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:02.940
It's not over between us!

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:09.220
That was a fine duel, Jonouchi boy.

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:16.600
That punk!

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:19.260
Pegasus!

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:24.640
You're very persistent.

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:27.000
Give me the prize money.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.340
If you don't, I'll end your life!

00:19:29.340 --> 00:19:32.660
You used to be the king of prize money.

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:39.640
Due to our previous duel, you've lost your duelist mentality.

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:41.350
Quit your blabbing!

00:19:41.350 --> 00:19:42.790
Where's the prize money?

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:45.820
The weak must leave.

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:10.520
After a brief recess, we'll begin the tournament's final match between Yugi Muto and Katsuya Jonouchi.

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:20.860
The time has finally come, Yugi.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:25.440
Jonouchi and I must duel each other.

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:37.540
They did it!  Yugi and Jonouchi made the finals!

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:41.140
Wait a second!  Does that mean they have to duel each other?

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:44.170
They can't!  They're best friends!

00:20:44.170 --> 00:20:47.080
Jonouchi, leave this to Yugi.

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:52.050
What?  You're battling with all your strength because you're best friends?

00:20:52.050 --> 00:20:56.970
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Finals of Friendship
Yugi vs Jonouchi (Part 1)

00:20:56.970 --> 00:20:58.620
Duel, standby!

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:12.040
The flask glistens

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:19.890
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:28.870
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:29.570 --> 00:21:36.640
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:38.340 --> 00:21:42.470
Shower of happiness

00:21:42.790 --> 00:21:46.590
I will shower you with it

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:54.860
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:59.100
Shower of happiness

00:21:59.360 --> 00:22:03.220
You are not alone

00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:09.940
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
